1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,060
Hi and welcome back to Act So far most of

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:08,220
the attention has been on understanding
yourself Now the view starts to

3
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:12,660
move outward Every day you move through
different parts of life and

4
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:16,840
in each one you have a role You may be a
student a family member

5
00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:20,720
a friend a neighbor an employee or
something else

6
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:25,480
These roles are not separate identities
They are different ways you

7
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:29,520
take part in the world around you
Understanding them helps you see not

8
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:33,700
only where you belong but also how your
actions connect you to other people

9
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:38,500
That connection is the starting point for
social awareness A role

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,620
is simply a position you take in a certain
part of life The same

11
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:46,880
person can have many roles in one day
Someone may be a student

12
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:50,880
in the morning a son or daughter at home a
friend later

13
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:55,400
and a customer at a shop None of these
roles cancels the

14
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,620
others They exist at the same time and
each one changes

15
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:03,860
what is expected in that situation This is
why two people can

16
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:07,900
live in the same place but experience it
differently they

17
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,760
may be connected to different people
responsibilities and communities

18
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:15,560
through the roles they have A role is not
just a label

19
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,860
it shapes how you participate Here is the
important part

20
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,580
roles usually come with responsibilities A
student is connected

21
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:28,760
to learning classmates and the school
environment A family member has

22
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,920
responsibilities toward people at home A
neighbor shares a space with other

23
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:37,060
people and affects that space through
everyday choices Knowing

24
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:41,260
your roles helps you notice these
connections It does not mean carrying

25
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:45,540
every problem around you It means
understanding that your actions happen

26
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:49,720
inside relationships and that each role
can affect other people in

27
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:53,860
small or large ways This is where social
awareness starts

28
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:58,060
to become practical Roles also help us
understand communities

29
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:02,520
A community can be thought of as people
who share something in common and

30
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,280
exist within a shared area or setting
Think about a school

31
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:11,380
students teachers and staff have different
roles but together they

32
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:15,480
form one community A family is another
community A

33
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:19,600
hospital can be another with doctors
nurses staff and patients

34
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:23,720
connected around a shared place and
purpose Your

35
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:27,820
roles are like doors Each one connects you
to a different community

36
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:31,500
and each community connects you to
different people and responsibilities

37
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:36,520
A community is more than a list of people
It also includes

38
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:39,940
the environment and things that make life
inside it possible

39
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:45,360
In a school that may include classrooms
learning materials facilities

40
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,080
rules and shared spaces In a hospital it
can include

41
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:54,280
medicine equipment rooms and systems that
support care

42
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,940
Looking at a community this way helps you
see it as a living system

43
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:04,300
People roles resources places and
relationships affect

44
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:08,400
one another When one part changes other
parts of the community may

45
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:12,540
feel the effect That is why community
problems are rarely

46
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:16,600
isolated Communities can also sit inside
larger

47
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:20,620
communities A class can be part of a
school A school can be part

48
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:24,480
of an education system A clinic can be
part of a hospital network

49
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:29,000
and that network can be part of a wider
health sector A neighborhood sits

50
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,360
inside a town or city which sits inside a
country

51
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:37,120
This is the extent of a community The
boundary depends on what you

52
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:41,100
were trying to understand Sometimes the
useful view is very small

53
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:45,300
Other times you need to step back and see
the larger system around it

54
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:50,060
Choosing the right scale makes the picture
clearer Once you know which

55
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:54,240
community you are looking at the next step
is to understand it instead

56
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:58,620
of guessing about it A simple
investigation can ask what issue

57
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:02,680
exists here Is it still happening Has
anyone tried to address it

58
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:06,920
before If so what did they do You do not

59
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:11,180
need to conduct formal research now Just
notice the habit behind these

60
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:15,580
questions When you want to understand a
community observation and

61
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:19,600
reliable information are more useful than
assumptions They help you

62
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,940
see what is actually happening before
deciding what it means

63
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:27,920
That habit will matter a lot in the next
unit So the path is

64
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:31,960
becoming clearer your roles connect you to
people

65
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:36,780
those roles carry responsibilities and
those connections place

66
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:40,820
you inside different communities Each
community has

67
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:44,700
its own people resources environment and
boundaries

68
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:49,680
In the next lesson we will look inside
those communities more

69
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:53,880
closely We will explore what contribution
and volunteering

70
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:57,500
mean how to notice both strengths and
problems

71
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:02,200
and how to build a simple community map
that leads directly into

72
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:06,440
the next unit Keep that map in mind That’s
it for today

73
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:08,180
and I’ll see you in the next lesson
